# Pre-Submission Reviewer (Cursor adapter)

This rule is a thin pointer. The actual agent is the skill in this repo —
read it and follow it as the orchestrator:

@skills/pre-submission-reviewer/SKILL.md

The nine subagents (system prompts) and the per-author profiles live in:

- `skills/pre-submission-reviewer/references/` — S-AB, S-IN, S-ME, S-RE, S-DI,
  S-CO, S-FD, S-RP, S-CD, the optional interactive `S-AV` (author verification
  quiz), plus `author_profile.md` and `review_manifest.md`.
- `skills/pre-submission-reviewer/profiles/` — voice profiles.

How to run it in Cursor (single agent, sequential — Mode B in the SKILL):

1. Load the prior review manifest (`reviews/<id>.review.json`) if it exists
   → reconciliation mode; otherwise iteration 1, a full review.
2. Gather inputs (manuscript, target journal, paper type) and calibrate.
3. On a re-review, run `scripts/detect_changes.py` on the author's latexdiff or
   before/after pair, then re-review only changed scope.
4. Process the registry one subagent at a time: read its reference file, apply
   only that checklist, emit its findings block, move on.
5. Synthesize into the 8-criterion rubric and write the report, ending with the
   AI-review disclosure stamp and the Ledger for next iteration.
6. (Optional) If asked to quiz/verify the authors, run the `S-AV` Author
   Verification pass (`references/section_author_verification.md`): examine one
   topic at a time (data/signal-processing first), record verbatim answers, and
   write the transcript + process-only in-paper statement. Never grade
   understanding — a named human adjudicates; it gates nothing.

Ground rules (non-negotiable): our group's own unpublished work only; advisory;
never write a referee report as if a human wrote it; disclose AI use; flag, don't
verify; iterations only improve (reconcile, never re-litigate unchanged text).
